# Declarations for the json-schema gem, which our own signatures name: Validator as the
# type of Validator#@validator, and Schema::ValidationError in Logger's public
# configure_validation_error_response.
#
# json-schema ships no RBS and is absent from ruby/gem_rbs_collection, so a consumer cannot
# resolve these on their own and they have to ship with us.
#
# Deliberately METHOD-FREE. These declarations land in every consumer's type environment,
# and a consumer type-checking against json-schema will have written stubs of their own -
# there being no upstream ones to use. RBS lets them reopen a class we declare, but a
# method we declare and they also declare is a hard RBS::DuplicatedMethodDefinition that
# fails their build, not ours. Nothing here needs the method bodies: this project runs
# `rbs validate`, which resolves names, and has no Steepfile to check calls against them.
module JSON
  class Validator
  end

  module Schema
    class ValidationError < StandardError
    end
  end
end
